  "lineage": "Lao lam saravane: Southern-Lao (Champasak-region) variant of the broader Lao lam (sung-and-spoken folk-narrative-and-courtship) tradition that includes the Thai cognate mor lam. Lam saravane is the lighter, more melodic-and-flirtatious variant compared to the heavier philosophical-and-narrative lam siphandone of the southernmost Lao region. Performance: lead singer (mor lam) with khaen bamboo-pipe-mouth-organ accompaniment, in extempore versified Lao-language verse-exchange with characteristic pentatonic-modal vocabulary and the rhythmic-pulsed khaen drone. The mid-twentieth-century Vientiane and Bangkok commercial-recording era spread the saravane variant nationally.",
